  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amar Subash Ghosh vs The State Of Maharashtra Thr. Pso, Ps, ... on 11 July, 2024 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Nagpur Bench : Nagpur Criminal Application (Aba) No.509 Of 2024 Amar Subash Ghosh Vs. State of Maharashtra, Through Police Station Officer, Police Station, Dhanora, District Gadchiroli ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Office Notes, Office Memoranda of Coram, appearances, Court's orders of directions and Registrar's orders ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- Mr. Madhur A. Deo, Advocate for applicant. Mrs. R. V. Sharma, App for respondent/State. Coram : Urm Dated : 11/ 1. Apprehending police in connect registered with Gadchiroli for the offences punishable 188, 273, 328 of the Indian Penal Code Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(iv), 30(2)(a), and 59(i) of the Food and Safety and St read with Section 2, 3 and 4 of the Foo Standards Rules, 2011, the applicant ap this Court for grant of pre-arrest bail 2. Moreover, whether in such types of cases, the application of Section 328 is proper or not Amar Subash Ghosh vs The State Of Maharashtra Thr. Pso, Ps, ... on 11 July, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/53877564/ 1 is pending before the Hon'ble Apex Court.",
    "facts": "He submitted that considering the allegations in the FIR the offence under Section 328 is not made out.",
    "arguments": "Now, the stock is already recovered, the custodial interrogation of the present applicant is not required, in view of that he be protected by granting ad-interim anticipatory bail. 3. Learned APP strongly opposed the said application on the ground that the huge stock of scented tobacco is recovered from the present applicant, in view of that, his custodial interrogation is required."
  },
